# ccci_rpcd reads a system property no vendor domain may read.
#
#   avc: denied { read } for comm="ccci_rpcd"
#     name="u:object_r:default_prop:s0" dev="tmpfs"
#     scontext=u:r:ccci_rpcd:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:default_prop:s0 tclass=file
#
# 2 records per boot. `default_prop` is the fallback label for an unlabelled
# SYSTEM property, and AOSP grants it to core and app domains only:
#
#   system/sepolicy/private/domain.te:88   get_prop(domain, core_property_type)
#                                          (not_compatible_property branch)
#
# ⚠ WHICH property is NOT identified, and the record cannot say -- a property
# read is audited against the context's backing file, never the property name.
# Tried, and failed to find it: intersecting the 45 properties that currently
# resolve to default_prop on the device against the string literals in
# /vendor/bin/ccci_rpcd and in the three libraries it loads that could read one
# (libsysenv.so, libccci_util.so, libhardware_legacy.so). No hit, which most
# likely means the property is simply not set on this device -- an unset
# property still requires access to the context file to come back empty.
#
# That also bounds the impact: whether the read is denied or allowed, ccci_rpcd
# gets nothing. The modem works -- SIM LOADED, both slots, data up.
#
# Silenced rather than granted. Granting a vendor domain read of default_prop
# means granting it every unlabelled system property at once, to fix a read that
# returns nothing.
dontaudit ccci_rpcd default_prop:file read;
